# 🏦 Distributed Banking System (gRPC Implementation)

## 📌 Overview
This repository contains a modern, high-performance distributed banking client-server application built using **gRPC** and **Protocol Buffers (Protobuf)**. By abstracting the network layer through HTTP/2, this implementation provides exceptional binary serialization performance, bi-directional capability, and tight contract enforcement.

---

## 📐 Protocol Specification & Contract

Unlike platform-dependent solutions, the entire communication layer, operational payload, and procedure signatures are strictly defined inside an IDL (Interface Definition Language) file: `src/main/proto/bank.proto`.

### 🗂️ Service Definition
```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";

option java_multiple_files = true;
option java_package = "bank.grpc";

service BankService {
  rpc Deposit (AmountRequest) returns (ActionResponse);
  rpc Withdraw (AmountRequest) returns (ActionResponse);
  rpc Transfer (TransferRequest) returns (ActionResponse);
  rpc QueryBalance (BalanceRequest) returns (BalanceResponse);
}
